cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the paper below and this software."
type: software
title: "Voice Negotiation Agents: Pipecat, LiveKit and GPT-Live negotiating freight rates in Spanish"
abstract: >-
  Code and data for an externally measured comparison of three voice-agent
  architectures that negotiate freight rates by phone in Mexican Spanish: two
  cascades (speech recognition, language model and speech synthesis) orchestrated
  by Pipecat and by LiveKit Agents, and OpenAI's GPT-Live speech model. Includes
  the three agents, the shared negotiation engine, prompt and tools, the harness
  that plays the carrier's recorded lines and measures latency on the listener's
  side, the simulated agents that validate it, the exported per-call and per-turn
  tables, and the scripts that regenerate every number in the paper.
